KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ namespace member hides global: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.lookup.general]/1, [basic.lookup.unqual]/1-2: unqualified
lookup stops at the first scope in which a declaration of the name is found.
For template names cpp_scopet::lookup_rec keeps collecting the templates of
the enclosing class and namespace scopes (it stops only at a block scope,
cpp_block_scope_using_declaration_hides_outer_template), so f<int>(0) in n
also sees the class template ::f and is a conversion error.
test_hidden_only_match.desc: accepts-invalid when the hidden template is
the only match.  Applying the rule everywhere broke libc++ <tuple>,
std::get and std::optional tests (round 163s notes).  Pre-existing (bin53).
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
